<!--
  Kuna: Itanium classes typed from the vtable graph and the code.
  P1 external-refinement (itaniumrtti); P0 assertion: option itaniumrtti off|on.

  The fixtures are stripped, hidden-visibility g++ builds, so only the Itanium
  RTTI graph names the classes, and nothing gives a size or a member.

  Asserts #1-#2 are the off pass: Shape::area is sub_14b8 reading its object
  as ((int *)a0)[2]. Asserts #3-#8 are the on pass: its `this` is a Shape *,
  laid out to the 0x10 bytes the deleting destructor passes to operator
  delete, so the read is this->field_0x8; Circle repeats its base's field and
  adds its own at 0xc; Circle's constructor stores &Circle_vptr into the typed
  vptr; and Vec<double>'s member, read through XMM0, is a double field, so its
  getter keeps returning double.
  Assert #9: Widget has two sub-vtables (Loggable and Drawable bases), so its
  methods keep an untyped receiver.
  Assert #10: Counter has no virtual destructor, so no operator delete gives its
  size; its method's receiver is only named `this`.
  Assert #11: Zero::zero returns a Zero by value through the slot in its first
  parameter, so that parameter is not `this`.
-->
